{
  "_comment": [
    "Lorenzo's scoping decision: which controls a software system can actually",
    "observe and enforce.",
    "",
    "IN  = the credit union's financial position, the transactions flowing through",
    "      the core, or the members themselves.",
    "OUT = organisational process \u2014 board governance, staff training, HR, policy",
    "      review calendars, vendor management workflow, internal audit process,",
    "      business continuity planning. These are REAL obligations discharged by",
    "      people and paperwork; building software to assert they happened is",
    "      theatre.",
    "",
    "Scoped-out controls are MARKED, never deleted, so the decision is reversible",
    "and the shape of the whole obligation stays legible. The out-of-scope count",
    "is reported next to the in-scope one for the same reason.",
    "",
    "`judgment_call: true` marks the controls that genuinely straddled the line",
    "(25 as of the 2026-07-19 rescope). Those are the ones to overrule first."
  ],
